WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.670
- [Instructor] In a previous video,

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:04.120
we figured out a way to
multiply a two-digit number

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.800
times one-digit number.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.920
What we did is we broke
up the two-digit numbers

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.410
in terms of its place value,
so the three here in the tenths

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.420
place that's three tens,
this is seven ones.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.251
So we view 37 sixes as the
same thing as 30 sixes,

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:21.251
three tens times six plus
seven sixes, seven times six.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.640
And then we added those
together to get a total of 222.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.370
What we'll try in this video
is now see what happens if we

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.539
try to do two digits times
two digits, so let's try

00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:38.539
to tackle 37, 37 instead of six
let's multiply that times 26

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.450
so we're trying to figure
out 37 26's is one way

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.530
to think about it.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.850
So pause this video and
see if you can tackle that

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.630
and see if you can maybe
use a similar method to what

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.603
we used before.

00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:54.450
Well one way to think about
it is you could view this

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.450
as 37 26's or you could view
this as 37 sixes plus 37 20's.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.130
So first we could do the 37
sixes which is exactly what

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:09.430
we did over here, we said hey
that's the same thing and we

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.190
could do it in either order
we could say hey let's first

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.810
think about 30 sixes, so we're
going to multiply 30 times

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.810
six 30 sixes is 180, so that
right over there is three tens

00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:25.080
times six.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.970
And then we could think about
the seven ones times six.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.010
And so that's going to be 42.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:37.037
That's the seven ones times
six or the seven sixes.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.500
And then we could do the same
thing with the 20's we could

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.500
say hey what are three tens,
what are 30 20's going to be.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.840
So let's write that over here
or you could say what are

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.260
three tens times two tens.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.130
Well that would be six times
ten times ten, so let me write

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.510
this down this is three tens
times two tens that's what

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.120
we're going to do now.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.450
Times two tens and that's
the same thing as which is

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.480
equal to 30 times 20 which
is the same thing as three

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.620
times two times ten times ten.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.850
Well that's going to be 600,
so we could write that here

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.756
600 and just be very clear,
we've already thought about

00:02:18.756 --> 00:02:21.392
37 sixes, that's these two
numbers up here we have to add

00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:24.480
that we still have to add them.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.060
But now we're thinking about
37 20's so first we thought

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.889
about 30 20's which is 600
and now we could think about

00:02:29.889 --> 00:02:34.889
seven 20's so seven 20's is
going to be seven times two

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.050
is 14 so seven times 20 is 140.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.300
So I'll write that right over here.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.300
140 to be clear this is
seven ones times two tens.

00:02:51.124 --> 00:02:54.917
Or seven 20's and now we
can add it all together

00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:57.150
to get what the total would be.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.440
So in the total we have,
that's why it's useful to have

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.640
everything stacked by their
place value, we could look

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.790
at the ones place so we say
okay we only have a total

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.010
of two ones here, so I'll put a two there.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.930
Now let's see tens we have
eight tens plus four tens

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.610
is 12 tens plus another
four tens is 16 tens.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.610
16 tens we can also break up
as 106 tens, so we could write

00:03:20.997 --> 00:03:23.690
the six tens here and
then put that 100 up here.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:28.690
So 100 plus another hundred
is 200 plus 600's is 800's

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.710
plus one more hundred is 900's.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.920
And so there you have
it, this is equal to 962.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.630
I really want you to
understand what we just did,

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.316
it might look a little bit
complicated but first we thought

00:03:40.316 --> 00:03:45.316
about what is 37 sixes that's
where we got these numbers

00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:48.120
from and that's what we had
done in a previous video.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.445
And then we just thought
about well what is 37 20's

00:03:51.445 --> 00:03:55.700
going to be and that's where
these numbers came from

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.054
and actually let me write that down.

00:03:58.054 --> 00:04:01.320
This whole thing that I'm
circling in orange, that is 37

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.320
sixes or I'll write it as 37
times six and then this is

00:04:07.925 --> 00:04:09.004
37 20's so 37 times 20.

00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:14.004
So if it's not obvious, pause
the video or after this video

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.580
reflect on why this works,
try it with other numbers

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.740
'cause if you really
understand this then your

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.900
multiplication life and
actually your mathematical lives

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.700
in your future will only
become more and more intuitive.

